---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
import { SITE_NAME, OPERATOR_NAME, PRICE } from "../config";
---
<Layout
  title="About Pool Compliance Melbourne | CertCycle"
  description="Pool Compliance Melbourne is a booking service operated by CertCycle. Learn how we work with independent, BPC-registered pool safety inspectors."
  path="/about/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: "About", path: "/about/" }]} />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-navy-900 mb-6">About {SITE_NAME}</h1>

    <div class="prose-content">
      <p class="text-lg">
        {SITE_NAME} is a booking service operated by {OPERATOR_NAME}. All inspections are performed by independent,
        BPC-registered pool safety inspectors.
      </p>

      <h2>What that means in practice</h2>
      <p>
        We don't employ inspectors directly, and we're not the ones physically checking your fence, gates or
        non-climbable zone. Instead, we act as the booking layer between pool and spa owners across Melbourne and a
        network of independent inspectors who each hold their own registration with the Building and Plumbing
        Commission (BPC), formerly the Victorian Building Authority. When you book with us, we confirm your details,
        match you with an available registered inspector in your area, and coordinate scheduling — typically within
        48 hours.
      </p>
      <p>
        This structure exists to make pool compliance simpler for owners, not more complicated. Instead of needing
        to independently research and vet individual inspectors, confirm their BPC registration, and negotiate
        pricing suburb by suburb, you get one consistent flat fee ({PRICE}), one clear process, and one point of
        contact for reminders about your 30-day lodgement deadline and four-year renewal — regardless of which
        registered inspector actually attends your property.
      </p>

      <h2>Why the distinction matters</h2>
      <p>
        Being upfront about this distinction matters because the Form 23 Certificate of Barrier Compliance is a
        legal document, and it can only be issued by an inspector who holds the correct BPC registration for pool
        barrier compliance specifically. We think it's important that owners understand exactly who is assessing
        their property and under what authority, rather than assuming a booking service and an inspection company
        are the same thing.
      </p>

      <h2>What we handle directly</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Taking your booking and confirming your suburb, pool or spa type, and preferred contact time.</li>
        <li>Coordinating scheduling with an available, BPC-registered inspector in your area.</li>
        <li>Providing one flat, transparent {PRICE} fee across all of greater Melbourne.</li>
        <li>Tracking your certificate's 30-day council lodgement deadline and sending you a reminder.</li>
        <li>Tracking your four-year renewal date and reminding you well ahead of your next required inspection.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the independent inspector handles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The physical, on-site barrier assessment — height, gaps, non-climbable zone, and gate function.</li>
        <li>Issuing your Form 23 Certificate of Barrier Compliance on the day, if your barrier passes.</li>
        <li>Providing a clear, specific list of any issues if your barrier doesn't pass, so they can be corrected before your free first re-inspection.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our approach to accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Victorian pool barrier requirements are specific and detailed, and they matter for genuine child safety
        reasons, not just paperwork compliance. Every guide and page on this site is written to reflect the current,
        general requirements accurately, and we'd rather state a general principle plainly than invent a specific
        detail we're not certain of. If you're ever unsure about how a rule applies to your particular property,
        your inspector is the right person to ask directly during your visit.
      </p>
    </div>

    <CTA />
  </div>
</Layout>
